# What the simulator changes about a Kode Dot build, applied last.
#
# Since esp-emu 1.1.0 the radio, the card and the panel are the board's own
# (the C5 runs in an esp-emu of its own), so almost nothing is left here.
#
# An older kode-sdk's link rest takes the DSI link down and, on the wake,
# reads the panel back through raw DSI packets; esp-emu answers a panel read
# with zeros. Only the link stays up; the rest itself - the glass dims, goes
# dark, DISPOFF/SLPIN - is as on the board. An SDK without the option (any
# from 0.1.1 on) ignores the line.
CONFIG_KODEOS_DISPLAY_SLEEP_LINK=n
